Excellent! This is the fix! The commit `3d261b9a` fixes the exact vulnerability. The fix adds `if (opt_pin == NULL)` before `free(pincode)`. This means the vulnerable version (our target) has:

```c
if (pincode && strlen((char *) pincode) == 0) {
    fprintf(stderr, "No PIN code supplied.\n");
    free(pincode);  // INVALID FREE if opt_pin is set to empty string
    return 2;
}
```

So the crash happens when `opt_pin` is set to an empty string. But as I analyzed, the fuzzer argv format can't represent an empty string directly...

